I never reward my pet any more.  When I have done, the result was that
it would pick up and drop items nearly every turn.  As it is, pets
spend more time picking up items than biting, which annoys me enough so
that I spend time cleaning the dungeon and hauling all the junk to the
nearest container (also making the container too heavy to pick up).

When I raid a shop, I pile all the non-food items along with a known
cursed item, then drop my gold to get credit.  With no other choice the
pet will eventually pick up the gold, at which point I leave the shop
and the pet follows me.  I repeat this until he drops the gold outside
the shop, then take the gold to build up more credit.  When I have
enough credit, I repeatedly buy and sell the shop's inventory to get
all the shopkeeper's gold.

